import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { repoBlob } from "../../lib/links.mjs";
---

<DocsLayout title="Configuration — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>Configuration</h1>
    <p class="lede">Use the target repository’s normal tools and your chosen interactive agent. Preserve existing accounts, models, permissions, and concurrency limits.</p>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Native prerequisites</h2>
<p>Read installed <code>hc --skill</code> and command help before native delegation. Confirm the current agent, actual lead identity, matching core, native status integration, and notifications. HC’s <code>notes = false</code> disables automatic notes.</p><p>For Codex, launch both lead and interactive helper with <code>--no-daemon</code>. Do not substitute a print-mode agent or change permissions to make a demonstration work.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("docs/native-hc.md")}> Native launch contract ↗</a></p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Working conventions</h2>
<p>Use one lead per workspace and one writer per checkout. Arrange separate Git worktrees for concurrent writers and stable inputs for checks and review. These are instructions, not a locking service.</p><p>A helper brief identifies its allowed scope, absolute worktree and procedure paths, report destination, required checks, permission for further delegation, and actual immediate-parent address.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Project checks and decisions</h2>
<p>Follow the project’s verification contract. Save important questions and the user’s actual answers in the task note; send follow-up through native HC. Status, helper messages, and tool output never expand user authority.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("templates/task.md")}> Task note ↗</a> <a href={repoBlob("AGENTS.md")}> Shared entry contract ↗</a></p>
</div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
